{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Moses in Midian.</b> Rabbi Avraham ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 4:19) that there is no chronological order in the Torah, and he explained it as meaning 'and He had already said,' and many instances are like this. But his words are not correct, for the first address did not take place in Midian but rather at Mount Sinai, and in Midian He spoke with him only this one time. Rather, when Moses accepted the mission to go by the word of HaShem and returned to Midian to obtain permission from his father-in-law, he intended to go stealthily, unrecognized. Therefore he said to him, 'Let me go now and return to my brothers who are in Egypt and see whether they are still alive' — meaning, I will see my brothers, whether they are still alive, and I will return, for this is the way of a brief visit to see one's brothers. <b>Then</b> YHWH said to him in Midian, 'Go, return to Egypt,' meaning, arise, leave this land and return to the land of Egypt, and do not fear there, <b>for all</b> those who sought your harm are dead, and you shall be there with the people until you bring them out from there. <b>Therefore</b> he took his wife and his sons, for this was sound counsel to bring them with him, because through this Israel would trust him more: for when he was a free man in Midian, sitting in his house in peace with his sons and with his wife the daughter of the priest of the land, he would not bring them to become a nation of slaves whose lives would be embittered with harsh labor — unless his heart was truly confident that they would soon depart and he would ascend with them to the land of Canaan, so that upon their departure he would not need to return to Midian to take his wife and his sons from there."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:02:45.774891352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}